# PEP 8 (Python)

Follow [PEP 8](https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/) for all Python in this session.

## Must

- 4-space indent; no tabs
- `snake_case` functions/vars; `CapWords` classes; `UPPER_SNAKE` constants
- Imports grouped: stdlib → third-party → local; one package per line preferred
- Spaces around operators and after commas; no trailing whitespace
- Prefer names that reveal intent; avoid 1-letter names except loop indices

## Soft

- Aim for ≤79 chars for pure style; ≤88–100 OK if project formatter (ruff/black) says so — match the repo tool if present
- Blank lines: 2 between top-level defs/classes; 1 between methods

## Do not

- Invent a conflicting house style when the repo has ruff/black/isort config — defer to project tooling, still keep PEP 8 naming/readability
